\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Random Number Generator\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs22 \cf0 This driver does one thing: generates a number between 1 and up to 20. \

\f0\b\fs26 Driver Properties\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs22 \cf0 Max Number:
\f1\b0  A random number is generated between 1 and the number you specify. Changing the max number does NOT generate a new random value.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sb200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs26 \cf0 Using the Driver\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs22 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Variables
\f1\b0 : RANDOM_NUMBER is the last number generated based on the property set at the time it was generated.\

\f0\b Events
\f1\b0 : The RandomNumberGenerated event runs every time a new number is generated. Note that you can also use the event of the RANDOM_NUMBER variable changing as well, but if the number generated is the same it will not trigger the action.\

\f0\b Actions
\f1\b0 : GenerateNewNumber action generates a new number and assigns it to the RANDOM_NUMBER variable.\

